WEBVTT

00:00.400 --> 00:05.918
Start in Pantry. Check what you already have before shopping. Open an item to review

00:05.918 --> 00:10.647
its amount or mark it running low. Your pantry reflects what you record.

00:15.400 --> 00:21.170
Open Shopping and add what is missing. Enter the item name, then an amount or store

00:21.170 --> 00:25.758
if useful. This is your shopping list, not extra pantry stock yet.

00:30.400 --> 00:36.103
After buying, open Expenses and scan the receipt. Use a clear photo with all item

00:36.103 --> 00:41.454
lines and the total. The scan is a draft. Nothing is saved just by scanning.

00:45.400 --> 00:50.939
Review the store, purchase date, total and currency. Keep Record in Expenses selected

00:50.939 --> 00:56.478
if you want the receipt recorded there. Correct mistakes against the original receipt

00:56.478 --> 00:57.390
before saving.

01:00.400 --> 01:06.321
Choose Add all for eligible items, or tap individual cards. Select food you keep at

01:06.321 --> 01:11.957
home. Leave meals eaten out, gifts and services unselected. Check each selected

01:11.957 --> 01:12.599
quantity.

01:15.400 --> 01:20.791
Open Quantity and matches for each receipt item. Review its Shopping item selection.

01:20.791 --> 01:26.117
Choose the matching pending item when appropriate, or save it as a new bought item.

01:30.400 --> 01:35.804
Review the final choices, then save and update pantry. If you already recorded this

01:35.804 --> 01:40.948
purchase, link the recent matching purchase when offered. That keeps its pantry

01:40.948 --> 01:42.901
amount from being added twice.

01:45.400 --> 01:50.740
Now check Expenses for spending, Shopping for the bought items, and Pantry for

01:50.740 --> 01:56.421
selected stock. Saving an expense alone does not add pantry items. You choose those

01:56.421 --> 01:57.927
updates during review.
